# Browser-automation debris. Page snapshots and console logs from driving the running app,
# which carry whatever was on screen plus absolute paths naming the developer's home
# directory. An `add -A` would stage them into a commit, so they are ignored rather than merely
# uncommitted.
.playwright-mcp/

# Agent tooling scratch
/.superpowers/
# Where the planning skills write working plans. By the owner's rule (2026-10-25) those are not
# kept in this repository; the requirements and design docs are.
/docs/superpowers/
# Both forms are deliberate. The trailing-slash form matches the directory this normally is.
# The bare form matches it when it is a symlink, which it became on 2026-10-22 when the ten
# worktrees were moved to /Volumes/MacMiniExt1 to recover internal disk. A directory-only
# pattern stops matching silently the moment the path becomes a symlink, and `git add -A` then
# stages a symlink pointing at an external volume into the repo. Verified with
# `git add -An .claude`: it staged .claude/worktrees before the bare form was added, and
# nothing after. Do not collapse these two lines into one.
/.claude/worktrees/
/.claude/worktrees
# Files agent tools generate in a clone. A clone's own .git/info/exclude does not travel to the
# next clone, so they are listed here. The bare form matches a file, a directory or a symlink
# alike, which is why these need one line each. They are listed by name, not as /.claude/*, so
# files meant to be shared (settings.json, skills, agents, agent-memory) can still be tracked.
/.claude/agent-memory-local
/.claude/agent-registry.json
/.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json
/.claude/checkpoints
/.claude/first-run
/.claude/mailbox
/.claude/routines/.state
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
/.claude/settings.local.json
